Ladybird’s tabs.removeCSS() removes the style sheets an insertCSS()
call added with the same code or file and the same cssOrigin, from the
frames the call names, through the same injection path as
scripting.removeCSS(). Firefox does the same, in
ExtensionTabsBase::removeCSS() (ext-tabs-base.js), which runs the
shared _execute() with a removeCSS flag. Chromium’s
TabsRemoveCSSFunction is an ExecuteCodeInTabFunction whose
ShouldRemoveCSS() returns true, and WebKit’s
WebExtensionContext::tabsRemoveCSS() takes the same injection
parameters as its insertCSS counterpart.
